# rl144 — a deterministic, integer-only roguelike written in Rust, built for the
# 486DX (terminal backend, static musl). Cross-built via the overlay ebuild using
# rustup nightly + -Zbuild-std (see Dockerfile + configs/overlay/games-roguelike/rl144).
games-roguelike/rl144

# GUI — the X server (SP-GUI G1). TinyX/kdrive Xfbdev: static, framebuffer-native,
# zero-dlopen, built over vesafb. Overlay ebuild pins the tinyx commit and pulls
# its server-side X libs (xorg-proto, libXfont v1, libfontenc, xtrans) as DEPENDs
# — they are NOT listed here (only the server is a world member). Bitmap-only, no
# freetype/fontconfig anywhere. Clients (dwm/st/dmenu) land in later milestones.
x11-base/monolith-xserver

# GUI — the X CLIENT stack (SP-GUI G2). The §2 client libs, cross+static, and
# NOTHING ELSE: xorg-proto (headers) + libxcb (+xcb-proto BDEPEND) + libX11 +
# libXext. dwm/st/dmenu link ONLY these — no Xt/Xaw/Xmu/ICE/SM, no Xft (bitmap
# core fonts only). libxcb/libXau/libXdmcp are pulled transitively by libX11 but
# listed here per spec §2 for intent. Each distinct client statically bakes its
# own libX11 (~1MB) — fewer resident clients = less RAM.
x11-base/xorg-proto
x11-libs/libxcb
x11-libs/libX11
x11-libs/libXext

# GUI — st, the suckless terminal (first §2 client). Ported off Xft/
# fontconfig/freetype entirely onto core X11 bitmap fonts (XLoadQueryFont /
# XDrawImageString16) — see configs/overlay/x11-terms/monolith-st and its
# files/st-0.9.2-core-fonts.patch. Links only libX11 + libXext, per the G2
# client-stack posture above. font-misc-misc supplies the default XLFD
# ("-misc-fixed-medium-r-normal--13-120-75-75-c-70-iso10646-1", 6x13 "fixed"
# in iso10646-1/Unicode) at runtime — st itself does not need it to build.
x11-terms/monolith-st
# media-fonts/font-misc-misc  # DEFERRED: added back after st's de-Xft compile is
# validated in isolation (runtime font only; separate cross concern — mkfontdir).

# Stele — a document-web browser for the 486 (Rust, one static binary, NO
# JavaScript by construction). Renders straight to /dev/fb0 (backend/fb.rs) with
# a compiled-in 8x8 bitmap font — needs neither X nor fonts on the disc. Cross-
# built via the overlay ebuild with rustup nightly + -Zbuild-std (Dockerfile +
# configs/overlay/www-client/stele). Actively developed → REPIN each build.
www-client/stele

# nethack — pinned to the last 3.6.x release. 5.0.0 (current ::gentoo head)
# requires USE=lua (REQUIRED_USE on lua_single_target_*) and restructured its
# util/Makefile build-variable names (MYCFLAGS/MYCXXFLAGS vs. this repo's
# CC_FOR_BUILD patch in configs/portage/bashrc, written for the 3.6.x shape).
# Pinning with '=' also stops any future epoch bump from silently floating
# this back up to 5.0.0 the way the unqualified atom did on 2026-08-02.
=games-roguelike/nethack-3.6.7-r1

# Module tools for the loadable-driver regime — modprobe/lsmod/depmod in the
# booted GNU rootfs (busybox's module applets are initramfs-only). Also gives
# the user `modprobe` at the shell: the drivers are on the disc; load what you like.
sys-apps/kmod
